# liquid-snipe — Provider Research

"Companion to PROJECT.md (Open decisions §) and SPEC.md (§5.6, §6, §11)."
"Resolves the two cost/latency-driving picks: gRPC stream AND SWQOS."
"Pricing as of May 2026. Tip floors and subscription tiers move month-to-month — re-verify before locking in."

## Operator profile

OperatorProfile {
  // Drives every pick below.

  location = "NY"
  "All region picks bias to NYC PoPs."

  cadence = "not full-time"
  "Goal: prove strategy works on paper, then trickle into live."
  "Don't pre-pay for predictable-cost infra (Helius Business, dedicated nodes) until expectancy measured."

  current = "Helius free tier"
  planned = "Triton PAYG ($125 entry) for real Yellowstone gRPC"

  avoid = "WS-fallback rung"
  "SPEC's logsNotifications + per-candidate getTransaction path adds 50-200ms per evaluation — kills the whole point of a sniper."
}

## TL;DR — Recommended day-one stack

DayOneStack {
  gRPC {
    pick           = "Triton One PAYG"
    monthly_fixed  = "$125 prepay → ~$60-300/mo metered after"
    per_tx         = "$0 per call, $0.08/GB egress"
    why            = "Cheapest real-Yellowstone path. Authors of yellowstone-grpc. NYC GeoDNS colocates to operator IP."
  }

  RPC {
    pick           = "Helius free (until rate-limited) → Helius Dev $49 if needed"
    monthly_fixed  = "$0"
    per_tx         = "$0"
    why            = "Already have it; upgrade only when free-tier RPS bites. Triton PAYG also covers RPC if consolidating."
  }

  SWQOS_slot_1 {
    pick           = "Jito (NYC)"
    monthly_fixed  = "$0"
    per_tx         = "live tip floor (~0.0000025 SOL p50, ~0.000337 SOL p99)"
    why            = "No account friction, only provider with bundles, lowest practical tip floor."
  }

  SWQOS_slot_2 {
    pick           = "0slot.trade (NY)"
    monthly_fixed  = "$0 (promo)"
    per_tx         = "0.0001 SOL (Advanced) / 0.001 SOL (lower tiers)"
    why            = "Parallel leg for fan-out, NY PoP, no approval gate."
  }

  SWQOS_slot_3_optional {
    pick           = "BlockRazor (NY)"
    monthly_fixed  = "$0"
    per_tx         = "0.0001 SOL"
    why            = "Best explicit anti-sandwich (sandwichMitigation + safeWindow) for fresh-pool buys."
  }
}

DayOneTotals {
  fixed     = "$125 Triton prepay (consumed as you stream, not lost)."
  recurring = "~$60-300/mo metered Triton + $0 RPC (until Helius free runs out) + variable SWQOS tips."
  intuition = "At 50 trades/day with Jito p75 tip ≈ $0.06/day at SOL=$200."
}

### Cost ladder

"When to step up, not where to start."

CostLadder {
  start {
    stack          = "Triton PAYG + Helius free + Jito (NYC)"
    monthly_fixed  = "~$60-300 metered"
    upgrade_when   = "— (this is the entry point)"
  }

  add_helius_dev {
    delta          = "+$49"
    upgrade_when   = "Helius free 429s on enrichment / blockhash refresh under sustained load"
  }

  add_parallel_swqos {
    stack          = "+ 0slot / BlockRazor as parallel SWQOS legs"
    delta          = "+$0"
    upgrade_when   = "First evidence of buy-failure correlation with single-provider latency"
  }

  swap_to_helius_business {
    stack          = "Swap Triton PAYG → Helius Business (flat)"
    monthly_fixed  = "$499"
    upgrade_when   = "Triton metered consistently above ~$400/mo AND you want predictable billing"
  }

  self_host_yellowstone {
    stack          = "Self-host Yellowstone in NYC (Latitude/Vultr)"
    monthly_fixed  = "~$800"
    upgrade_when   = "Monthly infra costs already > $500 AND strategy is profitably live full-time"
  }
}

"The point: don't pay for predictable-cost infra until the strategy proves itself."
"Triton PAYG aligns the bill with usage — slow weeks cost less, hot weeks cost more, no commitment to a flat tier."

## 1. gRPC providers

"One stream, 8 DEX program IDs, processed commitment."

interface GrpcProvider {
  name
  min_entry
  included
  regions
  latency
  auth
  gotcha
}

GrpcOptions {
  Helius_LaserStream {
    min_entry = "$499/mo (Business)"
    included  = "100M credits, 200 RPC req/s, multi-region failover, replay"
    regions   = "US / EU / Asia (managed)"
    latency   = "No published p99; managed gRPC ~few ms behind slot"
    auth      = "API key in URL"
    gotcha    = "Bandwidth add-on +$400/mo at high stream volume; chatty filters (Pump.fun) hit it fast."
  }

  Triton_DragonsMouth {
    min_entry = "$125 prepay (PAYG, metered after)"
    included  = "gRPC + WS streaming, replay (Old Faithful), Fumarole HA"
    regions   = "AMS + NYC (GeoDNS) — NYC matches operator"
    latency   = "Self-published: slot p90 ~5ms, account update p90 ~215ms"
    auth      = "x-token header"
    gotcha    = "$0.08/GB egress, $0/call for streaming — ~$60-300/mo for our 8-program filter. Region-pinning requires Dedicated (~$2,900/mo) but GeoDNS already routes NY traffic to NYC. account_include_max default 10 (we need 8 — fits)."
  }

  Jito_Shredstream {
    min_entry = "$0 + your infra (~1 vCPU, ~few hundred Mbps)"
    included  = "Raw shred UDP, up to 2 regions"
    regions   = "AMS, DUB, FRA, LON, NYC, SLC, SGP, TYO"
    latency   = "Lowest-latency feed on Solana; arrives BEFORE block assembly."
    auth      = "Pubkey whitelist (apply via Jito Discord)"
    gotcha    = "Shreds, NOT parsed tx — needs deshred → entry → tx → account-write resolution. Account state diffs not directly observable. Complement to Yellowstone, not substitute."
  }

  Self_hosted_Yellowstone {
    min_entry = "~$800/mo (Latitude f4.metal.large, FRA)"
    included  = "Full RPC + geyser-grpc-plugin, 20 TB egress pool"
    regions   = "Anywhere bare-metal exists"
    latency   = "Best possible — sub-ms plugin-to-consumer if colocated"
    auth      = "You configure (typically x-token)"
    gotcha    = "You now operate a Solana RPC node: monthly Agave releases, snapshots, peering, ~10-20 hr/mo sysadmin. Initial sync 6-24 hr."
  }
}

GrpcPick {
  pick = "Triton PAYG"
  "$125 prepay unlocks self-serve Yellowstone gRPC metered at $0.08/GB streaming with no per-call charge."
  "For our 8-program filter that's ~$60-300/mo — materially cheaper than Helius Business at $499 flat."
  "GeoDNS routes the operator's NY traffic to the NYC PoP, so shared-tier latency is fine for NY-based operation; no need to chase dedicated region-pinning."
  step_up_to_helius = "Only when Triton metered consistently exceeds the flat fee AND you want billing predictability."
  self_host         = "A 'strategy is profitably full-time' decision, not a day-one one."
  shredstream       = "Insufficient alone — delivers raw shreds, not the parsed account writes the hot loop needs."
}

## 2. SWQOS providers

"The bot's [[swqos]] array can hold any combination. Concurrent multi-provider sends use the SDK's parallel-submit path (fastest wins)."
"Cost equation: monthly subscription + per-tx tip floor × trade rate."

interface SwqosProvider {
  name
  monthly_fee
  min_tip
  regions
  transports
  bundles
  mev_protect
  self_host
  onboarding
  verdict
}

SwqosOptions {
  Jito {
    monthly_fee = "$0"
    min_tip     = "1k lamports floor; live p50 ~0.0000025 SOL, p99 ~0.000337 SOL"
    regions     = "AMS, DUB, FRA, LON, NYC, SLC, DAL, SGP, TYO"
    transports  = ["HTTP", "gRPC"]
    bundles     = "Yes (5-tx atomic, revert protect)"
    mev_protect = "default on single-tx"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "instant, no key required"
    verdict     = "enable"
  }

  Zero_slot_trade {
    monthly_fee = "$0 (promo)"
    min_tip     = "0.001 SOL (Trial/Entry/Inter) / 0.0001 SOL (Advanced)"
    regions     = "NY, LA, FRA, AMS, TYO"
    transports  = "HTTP staked_conn"
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "claimed best-in-class anti-sandwich"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "Discord (kurt0slot) — friction"
    verdict     = "enable as 2nd leg"
  }

  BlockRazor {
    monthly_fee = "$0"
    min_tip     = "0.0001 SOL (T0) / 0.001 SOL (T4-T1)"
    regions     = "NY, FRA, AMS, LON, TYO"
    transports  = ["HTTP", "gRPC"]
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "explicit sandwichMitigation + safeWindow"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "API key"
    verdict     = "enable as 3rd leg for fresh-pool buys"
  }

  Astralane {
    monthly_fee = "unpublished (sales)"
    min_tip     = "0.00001 SOL (lowest)"
    regions     = "FRAx2, SF, TYO, NY, AMSx2, Limburg, SGP, Lithuania"
    transports  = ["HTTP /iris", "Binary /irisb", "QUIC :7000 / :9000 (mev-protect)"]
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "port 9000 + mev-protect=true flag"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "sales contact required"
    verdict     = "evaluate — opaque price but tech is best-in-class (persistent QUIC, lowest tip)"
  }

  Temporal_Nozomi {
    monthly_fee = "$0 (gated approval)"
    min_tip     = "0.001 SOL (~1000x Jito floor)"
    regions     = "PIT, EWR, IAD, LA, FRA, AMS, LON, TYO, SGP"
    transports  = "HTTP"
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "optional Front-Running Protection (Helius/Coinbase only — slower)"
    self_host   = "enterprise-only"
    onboarding  = "approval form"
    verdict     = "skip day one — same floor as 0slot, no compensating advantage. Only consider for US-east coverage 0slot lacks."
  }

  NextBlock {
    monthly_fee = "$249/mo (Entry, 5 TPS)"
    min_tip     = "0.001 SOL"
    regions     = "NY, FRA, AMS, DUB, SLC, TYO, SGP, LON"
    transports  = "HTTP"
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "not documented"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "API key"
    verdict     = "skip — only one with mandatory subscription, steep for solo wallet."
  }

  FlashBlock {
    monthly_fee = "unpublished (sales)"
    min_tip     = "0.0001 SOL"
    regions     = "NY, SLC, AMS, FRA, LON, SGP, TYO"
    transports  = "HTTP"
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "claimed but no toggle documented"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "sales contact"
    verdict     = "skip — no transparent pricing, no QUIC, weak MEV story, obscure."
  }

  SpeedLanding {
    monthly_fee = "private"
    min_tip     = "0.001 SOL"
    regions     = "NYC, FRA, AMS, TYO, SGP"
    transports  = "QUIC :17778 only"
    bundles     = false
    mev_protect = "not documented"
    self_host   = false
    onboarding  = "wallet-pubkey-bound, contact via fnzero"
    verdict     = "skip — effectively private, no self-serve onboarding."
  }
}

### Per-tx cost intuition

"SOL = $200."

CostIntuition {
  astralane         = "0.00001 SOL → $0.002/tx → $0.20 / 100tx"
  cheap_tier        = "0.0001 SOL  → $0.02/tx  → $2.00 / 100tx  (0slot Adv, BlockRazor T0, FlashBlock)"
  jito_competitive  = "0.0003 SOL  → $0.06/tx  → $6.00 / 100tx  (Jito p99)"
  high_tier         = "0.001 SOL   → $0.20/tx  → $20.00 / 100tx (Nozomi, NextBlock, 0slot lower tiers)"
}

"Subscription-vs-tip math kills NextBlock for a solo wallet: $249/mo + $20 per 100tx vs Jito's $0/mo + $6 per 100tx."
"NextBlock only wins if you're routinely above ~1500 tx/mo AND their 5 TPS rate limit matters — neither holds for our profile."

## 3. Open questions

OpenQuestions {
  Q1_JitoTipFloor {
    "SPEC §6 has [gas] static fields. We need a live-tip-floor poll feeding the buy executor — otherwise we either underbid (no land) or overpay."
    endpoint = "https://bundles.jito.wtf/api/v1/bundles/tip_floor"
    action   = "Add a small task in bg/blockhash.rs neighborhood that refreshes the Jito tip percentile every N seconds and exposes it as AtomicU64 jito_tip_lamports. Probably p75 by default, configurable."
  }

  Q2_AstralaneOnboarding {
    "If pricing turns out to be reasonable (~$2-3/mo indexing tier suggests sender plans are similar), it's the strongest tech pick: lowest tip floor, persistent QUIC eliminates handshake on every submit, dedicated MEV-protect port."
    action = "Request a quote before committing to BlockRazor as the third leg."
  }

  Q3_ZeroSlotPromoEndDate {
    "0slot 'Free!' is flagged 'NEW' — could revert any time. Validate when re-checking pricing."
  }

  Q4_NozomiUSEastCoverage {
    "If we discover that US-east leader slots matter (verify by slot-vs-region analysis once live), Nozomi's PIT/EWR/IAD PoPs are the only ones in our provider set."
    cost = "Same 0.001 SOL floor as 0slot Trial."
  }

  Q5_SelfHostedYellowstoneBreakEven {
    "Not relevant until the strategy is profitably full-time."
    trigger_to_revisit = "Monthly infra > $500/mo AND live PnL justifies the ~10-20 hr/mo ops burden."
    box = "NYC (Latitude m3.large.x86 or comparable) — same region as the operator and most NY-side leader stake."
  }

  Q6_TritonBandwidthCeiling {
    "PAYG bills overage at the same base rate ($0.08/GB), so there's no cliff — but a runaway filter (e.g. accidentally subscribing to a chatty system program) could rack up a surprise bill."
    action = "Set a budget alert in Triton console; cap the filter to the 8 confirmed DEX program IDs; validate egress for the first week."
  }
}

